course: dictionary
lesson: 11276
title: Wrinkly: full of creases, and one rude slang word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wrinkly means having lots of wrinkles or creases, the little folds that show up on skin or cloth. Your fingers go wrinkly after a long bath, and a shirt goes wrinkly when it is squashed in a suitcase. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: In a story, «Grandma's wrinkly smile» tells you Grandma is old, and words like smile show it is a kind, warm way of saying so. Wrinklier and wrinkliest are the comparing forms: «a wrinklier shirt» is more creased than another shirt.
explain: Watch out for the slang noun. In the UK, some people say «the wrinklies» to mean old people, but it is rude and can hurt feelings. Ask yourself: is the tone warm, or unkind?
fact: Wrinkly means having many wrinkles or creases.
fact: The comparing forms are wrinkly, wrinklier and wrinkliest.
fact: «Your brain is a soft, wrinkly organ about 1.4 kilograms in an adult.»
fact: «Every living body slowly wears out as the years go by: skin gets thinner and wrinkly.»
fact: In UK slang, a wrinkly is an old person, and it can be unkind, so it is best left out of your own speech.
exercise: «Her hands were soft and wrinkly after the long bath.» What does wrinkly mean here? | Loud and noisy | Clean and shiny | *Having many small creases | Very cold and frozen
exercise: «Grandma's wrinkly smile» shows she is what? | Angry and rude | Hungry | *Old, in a warm and kind way | Very tall
exercise: Which word means more creased than something else? | wrinkle | *wrinklier | wrinkliest | windy
test: «The shirt came out of the suitcase all wrinkly.» What does wrinkly mean? | Clean and ironed | *Full of creases | Wet and dripping | Bright red
test: Some UK people use the slang word «wrinklies». Why should you be careful with it? | *It can be rude and hurt feelings | It is a word for a new baby | It means a fun game | It is the name of a fish
exam: «The wrinkly folds along its sides give it more skin.» What do the folds give the giant salamander? | Colour | Wings | Four toes | *More skin
